+  //
+  // Cross-origin sheets throw SecurityError on .cssRules even though
+  // they are genuinely applied - standard same-origin policy, not a
+  // bug - and are skipped. That risks a false negative for a page
+  // whose only safe-area CSS lives in an inaccessible sheet, which is
+  // preferred over guessing true and putting a reserved strip behind
+  // the pill on pages that do not want one.
+  // Runs a script against the page, as page script rather than chrome
