+              // at all when the inset was reported correctly, because it
+              // never reads the variable - such a page needs the layout
+              // viewport shortened instead. Cross-origin sheets mean
+              // this cannot distinguish "does not use env()" from "uses
+              // it where we cannot see it", so the app treats a bar as
+              // the weaker signal and shortens the viewport, which moves
+              // page content either way.
+              return { usesSafeAreaInset: false, hasBottomBar: true };
